Most banks store money.
But what if your money determined how much data you could store?

Today, I stepped into the role of a data analyst while working on Case Study 4: Data Bank from the SQL 8 Week Challenge.

Data Bank isn’t just a digital bank, it also offers secure cloud storage.
And here’s the twist:
The more money a customer has, the more data they can store.

Sounds simple…until you try to answer:
How much storage will customers need in the future?
What happens as customer numbers grow?
Are resources being used efficiently?

My task?
To help the management team make sense of their data...Analyzing customer financial activity and usage patterns to forecast future data storage demand.

Excited to uncover patterns, calculate key metrics, and turn data into actionable insights!

